{
    "dataType": "CVE_RECORD",
    "dataVersion": "5.2",
    "cveMetadata": {
        "cveId": "CVE-2026-99366",
        "assignerOrgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
        "state": "PUBLISHED",
        "assignerShortName": "Linux",
        "dateReserved": "2026-09-25T10:25:14.410Z",
        "datePublished": "2026-11-19T14:22:57.262Z",
        "dateUpdated": "2026-11-23T08:01:59.464Z"
    },
    "containers": {
        "cna": {
            "providerMetadata": {
                "orgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
                "shortName": "Linux",
                "dateUpdated": "2026-11-23T08:01:59.464Z"
            },
            "descriptions": [
                {
                    "lang": "en",
                    "value": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: don't modify a session slot when replaying its cached reply\n\nnfsd4_sequence() claims a session slot by setting NFSD4_SLOT_INUSE\nunder nn->client_lock. A reply served from the slot's reply cache does\nnot claim it, and that distinction lived only in cstate->status, which\nnfsd4_sequence() set to nfserr_replay_cache. Commit cc028a10a48c\n(\"NFSD: Hoist status code encoding into XDR encoder functions\") moved\nnfsd4_proc_compound()'s cstate->status assignment below the out:\nlabel, and the replay path's goto out was the one path that relied on\nskipping it. The test in nfsd4_sequence_done() therefore no longer\nidentifies a replay, and every replay now stores its reply and clears\nNFSD4_SLOT_INUSE as though it owned the slot.\n\nNFSD4_SLOT_INUSE is the interlock: check_slot_seqid() rejects every\nsequence id for a slot that is in use, before replay_matches_cache()\nruns. A replay never sets it, so two replays can be in flight on the\nsame slot at once. One can read slot->sl_cred under nn->client_lock\nwhile the other's completion frees and rebuilds it from the XDR\nencoder without that lock. Two completions can also collide with each\nother and release the same group_info twice. free_svc_cred() leaves\ncr_uid, cr_gid and cr_flavor intact, so the reader passes every\nearlier test in same_creds() and dereferences a NULL cr_group_info.\nFrom a 6.12.91 production server:\n\n  BUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference, address: 0000000000000004\n  CPU: 63 UID: 0 PID: 39015 Comm: nfsd\n  RIP: 0010:same_creds+0x38/0xa0 [nfsd]\n  RDX: 0000000000000000\n  Call Trace:\n   nfsd4_sequence+0x6a8/0x910 [nfsd]\n   nfsd4_proc_compound+0x345/0x670 [nfsd]\n   nfsd_dispatch+0x100/0x220 [nfsd]\n   svc_process_common+0x311/0x700 [sunrpc]\n   svc_process+0x131/0x1c0 [sunrpc]\n   svc_recv+0x7ef/0x9c0 [sunrpc]\n   nfsd+0xa3/0x100 [nfsd]\n  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception\n\nSince v6.14 a live session's slot table can shrink, and the unowned\nstore becomes a use-after-free write. nfsd4_sequence() defers the\nshrink while a slot is in use, but it tests NFSD4_SLOT_INUSE, which a\nreplay does not set, so free_session_slots() can kfree() the slot the\nreplay still holds in cstate->slot.\n\nRecord the claim in cstate->slot_owned when nfsd4_sequence() accepts a\nrequest and test that in nfsd4_sequence_done(), so only the request\nthat claimed the slot updates its cached reply and clears\nNFSD4_SLOT_INUSE. svc_generic_init_request() zeroes the compound\nresponse before each request, so the flag starts clear."
                }
            ],
            "metrics": [
                {
                    "cvssV3_1": {
                        "version": "3.1",
                        "vectorString": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H",
                        "baseScore": 9.8,
                        "baseSeverity": "CRITICAL"
                    },
                    "scenarios": [
                        {
                            "lang": "en",
                            "value": "AV:N - The attacker sends an NFSv4.1 COMPOUND whose first operation is OP_SEQUENCE, carrying sessionid, slotid, and seqid, over TCP. nfsd_dispatch() calls nfsd4_proc_compound(), which calls nfsd4_sequence(); when seqid equals slot->sl_seqid the replay path runs, and nfs4svc_encode_compoundres() calls nfsd4_sequence_done() on that slot.\nAC:L - The replay arm of nfsd4_sequence() never sets NFSD4_SLOT_INUSE, and check_slot_seqid() rejects another SEQUENCE for the slot only while that flag is set. The attacker sends two overlapping COMPOUND replays of one slot seqid, so both calls reach nfsd4_store_cache_entry() and free_svc_cred() on the same slot->sl_cred.\nPR:N - svcauth_unix_accept() copies the RPC_AUTH_SYS uid, gid, and supplementary groups from the call and checks only an AUTH_NULL verifier. The attacker uses that asserted identity for EXCHANGE_ID, CREATE_SESSION, and the replayed OP_SEQUENCE; nfsd4_sequence() accepts it with no capability or GSS check.\nUI:N - The attacker completes the attack by sending EXCHANGE_ID, CREATE_SESSION, and the overlapping SEQUENCE replays on its own connections.\nS:U - Impact is confined to the kernel that handled the COMPOUND, the same security authority as the corrupted nfsd4_slot and its embedded svc_cred.\nC:H - free_svc_cred() releases slot->sl_cred.cr_group_info without nn->client_lock while another replay, in replay_matches_cache(), calls same_creds() and groups_equal() on that pointer. groups_equal() reads ngroups and gid[] from a group_info that put_group_info() may already have passed to groups_free().\nI:H - Both replay completions call free_svc_cred() on one slot->sl_cred, so both call put_group_info() on its cr_group_info; groups_free() kvfrees it while the other completion still uses it. A replay also leaves NFSD4_SLOT_INUSE unset, so after nfsd_slot_shrinker_scan() lowers se_target_maxslots, free_session_slots() can kfree the slot and nfsd4_store_cache_entry() writes sl_cred and sl_data through the dangling cstate->slot.\nA:H - init_svc_cred() in free_svc_cred() clears cr_group_info but leaves cr_uid, cr_gid, and cr_flavor, so same_creds() passes those checks and groups_equal() dereferences NULL. That oops is the fatal nfsd exception reported from nfsd4_sequence()."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ],
