    "dataVersion": "5.2",
    "cveMetadata": {
        "cveId": "CVE-2026-99383",
        "assignerOrgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
        "state": "PUBLISHED",
        "assignerShortName": "Linux",
        "dateReserved": "2026-09-25T10:25:14.411Z",
        "datePublished": "2026-11-19T14:23:23.299Z",
        "dateUpdated": "2026-11-22T11:07:57.952Z"
    },
    "containers": {
        "cna": {
            "providerMetadata": {
                "orgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
                "shortName": "Linux",
                "dateUpdated": "2026-11-22T11:07:57.952Z"
            },
            "descriptions": [
                {
                    "lang": "en",
                    "value": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: reclaim credits for decrypted reads with no matching mid\n\nWhen a decrypted SMB2 READ response carries a MessageId that matches no\noutstanding request, both the inline receive_encrypted_read() and the\noffloaded smb2_decrypt_offload() paths drop the frame without accounting\nthe credits the server granted in it.  The plaintext unknown-frame path in\ncifs_demultiplex_thread() already reclaims them with\nsmb2_add_credits_from_hdr(), so encrypted reads leak credits that the\nplaintext path would not.\n\nThis also happens for legitimate frames - e.g. a reply that arrives after\nthe client has timed out and dropped the mid - so over a long-lived\nconnection the client's credit count drifts down and can eventually starve\nit of the ability to issue requests.  The frame is AEAD-authenticated, so\nthe granted credits in the decrypted header come from the real server and\nare safe to apply.\n\nReclaim the credits from the decrypted header before dropping the frame,\nand export smb2_add_credits_from_hdr() so the SMB2 receive paths can use it."
                }
            ],
            "metrics": [
                {
                    "cvssV3_1": {
                        "version": "3.1",
                        "vectorString": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                        "baseScore": 7.5,
                        "baseSeverity": "HIGH"
                    },
                    "scenarios": [
                        {
                            "lang": "en",
                            "value": "AV:N - cifs_demultiplex_thread reads the server SMB2 transform PDU from the TCP socket, and smb3_receive_transform hands frames larger than CIFSMaxBufSize to receive_encrypted_read. A decrypted smb2_hdr.MessageId that misses smb2_find_mid drops the CreditRequest grant on that wire response.\nAC:L - The server sets SMB2_SESSION_FLAG_ENCRYPT_DATA or SHI1005_FLAGS_ENCRYPT_DATA so smb3_encryption_required is true, then sends one transform READ whose MessageId is not a MID_REQUEST_SUBMITTED entry on pending_mid_q. decrypt_raw_data succeeds with the server's session key and the missed credit update is immediate.\nPR:N - receive_encrypted_read and smb2_decrypt_offload run in cifsd after decrypt_raw_data and never consult the local task's uid or capabilities. The peer that holds the SMB3 session keys is the server the client connected to.\nUI:N - On an established session the server alone writes the encrypted SMB2 READ response; cifs_demultiplex_thread processes that PDU from the socket without a further local mount or read.\nS:U - The lost accounting is TCP_Server_Info.credits for the SMB session whose socket received the frame, the same kernel scope as cifsd.\nC:N - The NULL-mid path in receive_encrypted_read and smb2_decrypt_offload only logs and frees the decrypted buffer; READ payload is not copied to a caller or to any other kernel object.\nI:N - The defect is skipping smb2_add_credits_from_hdr, so smb2_hdr.CreditRequest is not added to server->credits. That path stores nothing into file data or other kernel objects.\nA:H - smb2_readv_callback zeroes rdata->credits and replenishes server->credits only from smb2_hdr.CreditRequest. Dropping that grant in receive_encrypted_read or smb2_decrypt_offload shrinks the pool until wait_for_free_request sleeps in wait_for_free_credits with timeout -1 and new SMB commands cannot be sent."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ],
