    "containers": {
        "cna": {
            "providerMetadata": {
                "orgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
                "shortName": "Linux",
                "dateUpdated": "2026-11-23T08:02:33.650Z"
            },
            "descriptions": [
                {
                    "lang": "en",
                    "value": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\novl: use the pinned upper dir in ovl_fix_origin()\n\nRenames made directly on the upper filesystem during a lookup crash the\nkernel.\n\nA dentry that is passed to vfs_setxattr() must be pinned.\novl_fix_origin() passes upper->d_parent to ovl_set_impure() without a\nreference, and the lookup holds no lock of the upper directory. A\nrename on the upper filesystem changes d_parent, and only the child\npins the new parent, so a second rename and an rmdir free it.\n\nWith delays in ovl_fix_origin() and ovl_set_impure(), renaming the upper\ndirectory twice and removing the intermediate parent during the lookup\nof a merge directory without an origin xattr gave a KASAN\nuse-after-free in vfs_setxattr().\n\nFix this by passing the upper dentry that the overlay parent holds.\n\n[amir: add helper ovl_set_impure_dir()]"
                }
            ],
            "metrics": [
                {
                    "cvssV3_1": {
                        "version": "3.1",
                        "vectorString": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H",
                        "baseScore": 7.8,
                        "baseSeverity": "HIGH"
                    },
                    "scenarios": [
                        {
                            "lang": "en",
                            "value": "AV:L - ovl_fix_origin() is called from ovl_lookup() (overlay directory ->lookup, via __lookup_slow() on a path walk) and passes upper->d_parent to ovl_set_impure(). That parent is freed by two rename()s of the upper dentry plus rmdir() of the intermediate directory on the upper filesystem.\nAC:L - The attacker builds a merge directory with no origin xattr, then runs the lookup together with the two upper rename()s and the rmdir(). lookup_one_unlocked() has already dropped the upper directory i_rwsem, and both sides of the race are the attacker's own syscalls.\nPR:L - Search access on the overlay and write access on the upper directory are sufficient. overlayfs sets FS_USERNS_MOUNT, and a userxattr mount in an unprivileged user namespace leaves noxattr false, so ovl_fix_origin() runs on directories that user owns.\nUI:N - The attacker creates the layers, mounts overlay, walks the merge directory into ovl_fix_origin(), and performs the upper rename and rmdir themselves.\nS:U - ovl_set_impure() feeds the freed upper parent to vfs_setxattr() in the kernel that is handling the attacker's lookup and rename, so the corruption is a local kernel privilege escalation.\nC:H - vfs_setxattr() reads dentry->d_inode and the inode's xattr handlers from the upper parent after rmdir has freed that dentry. Reclaiming the dentry-cache object exposes the replacement's kernel pointers to this path.\nI:H - vfs_setxattr() calls inode_lock() and handler->set() on the freed upper parent's d_inode. A reclaimed dentry-cache slot gives that path a kernel write through the corrupted inode.\nA:H - Freeing the unpinned upper parent while ovl_set_impure() is inside vfs_setxattr() is the KASAN use-after-free reported for this bug and oopses on the dead dentry."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ],
