{
    "dataType": "CVE_RECORD",
    "dataVersion": "5.2",
    "cveMetadata": {
        "cveId": "CVE-2026-99424",
        "assignerOrgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
        "state": "PUBLISHED",
        "assignerShortName": "Linux",
        "dateReserved": "2026-09-25T10:25:14.414Z",
        "datePublished": "2026-11-19T14:40:27.661Z",
        "dateUpdated": "2026-11-23T08:02:35.820Z"
    },
    "containers": {
        "cna": {
            "providerMetadata": {
                "orgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
                "shortName": "Linux",
                "dateUpdated": "2026-11-23T08:02:35.820Z"
            },
            "descriptions": [
                {
                    "lang": "en",
                    "value": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\novl: set OVL_WHITEOUTS before publishing the upper dir\n\nListing a directory while it is copied up causes a use-after-free of\nthe readdir cache.\n\nA merge directory must never be iterated as a real upper directory:\nthat mode frees the cache in OVL_I(inode)->cache without looking at\nits refcount, while files opened in merged mode still use it.\novl_copy_up_workdir() publishes the upper dentry before it sets\nOVL_WHITEOUTS, and ovl_dir_open() samples both without a lock, so an\nopen between the two stores finds the upper directory and takes it\nfor a real one.\n\nWith a delay between the two stores, an unprivileged process that\nlisted a directory during its copy-up saw only \".\" and \"..\", and its\nnext getdents freed the readdir cache of another descriptor.\n\nFix this by setting OVL_WHITEOUTS before ovl_inode_update(), so that\novl_dir_reset() agrees with ovl_dir_open(), and by testing\nOVL_TYPE_MERGE() of the path type in ovl_dir_open(), so that an open\nthat observes the upper dentry never iterates a merge dir as a real\ndir, regardless of the order in which it observes the flag.\n\n[amir: test OVL_TYPE_MERGE() instead of smp_rmb() in ovl_dir_open()]"
                }
            ],
            "metrics": [
                {
                    "cvssV3_1": {
                        "version": "3.1",
                        "vectorString": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H",
                        "baseScore": 7.8,
                        "baseSeverity": "HIGH"
                    },
                    "scenarios": [
                        {
                            "lang": "en",
                            "value": "AV:L - open() reaches the patched ovl_dir_open() through do_dentry_open(), and getdents64() reaches ovl_iterate() through iterate_dir(), racing ovl_copy_up_workdir(). creat(), open(O_WRONLY), and chmod() enter that function via ovl_copy_up(), ovl_copy_up_one(), and ovl_do_copy_up().\nAC:L - The same caller runs the copy-up and the racing open/getdents. ovl_copy_up_workdir() stored __upperdentry in ovl_inode_update() and only afterwards set_bit(OVL_WHITEOUTS); ovl_dir_open() read ovl_path_real() and ovl_dir_is_real() with neither i_rwsem nor OVL_I(inode)->lock held, so repeating that pair hits the window.\nPR:L - ovl_permission() authorizes the directory owner through generic_permission() and checks no capability. That user can open and getdents the directory, and can force ovl_copy_up() from ovl_create(), from ovl_maybe_copy_up() on a write open, or from ovl_setattr() when chmod or chown touches a file they own.\nUI:N - The attacker personally issues open, getdents64, and the create, write-open, or chmod that calls ovl_copy_up() on a single-lower directory that does not yet have an upper.\nS:U - The object freed is the overlay directory cache OVL_I(inode)->cache in the kernel that handled the getdents. Turning that use-after-free into code execution is privilege escalation in that same kernel.\nC:H - A real-mode getdents takes ovl_iterate_real() into ovl_cache_get_impure(), which ovl_dir_cache_free()s OVL_I(inode)->cache and its ovl_cache_entry list without reading refcount. The other fd's ovl_iterate_merged() then dir_emit()s p->name and p->len from that freed entry into the getdents64 buffer.\nI:H - ovl_iterate_merged() writes the freed ovl_cache_entry: ovl_cache_update() stores p->ino and p->is_whiteout, and the cursor follows p->l_node.next. After the slab is reused those stores corrupt the object that now occupies the entry.\nA:H - ovl_dir_cache_free() kfree()s the ovl_dir_cache while another descriptor's od->cache still points at it. The next ovl_iterate_merged() dereferences od->cache->entries and the freed ovl_cache_entry list, which oopses the kernel."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ],
