    "containers": {
        "cna": {
            "providerMetadata": {
                "orgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
                "shortName": "Linux",
                "dateUpdated": "2026-11-23T08:03:38.600Z"
            },
            "descriptions": [
                {
                    "lang": "en",
                    "value": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm/hugetlb: fix use-after-free in hugetlb_mfill_atomic_pte()\n\nLet's fix another instance where we use a folio after dropping the PTL,\nwhere someone else could e.g., MADV_DONTNEED it once we drop the PTL,\nmaking us trigger a use-after-free on the folio."
                }
            ],
            "metrics": [
                {
                    "cvssV3_1": {
                        "version": "3.1",
                        "vectorString": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H",
                        "baseScore": 7.8,
                        "baseSeverity": "HIGH"
                    },
                    "scenarios": [
                        {
                            "lang": "en",
                            "value": "AV:L - UFFDIO_COPY reaches hugetlb_mfill_atomic_pte() via userfaultfd_copy(), mfill_atomic_copy(), and mfill_atomic_hugetlb(); the folio used after spin_unlock(ptl) is the private huge page that ioctl installed, not a field taken from a received packet.\nAC:L - The caller races UFFDIO_COPY with MADV_DONTNEED on a MAP_PRIVATE|MAP_NORESERVE hugetlb VMA, or in the child after fork(), where __vma_private_lock() is false. hugetlb_vma_lock_read() is then a no-op, so hugetlb_unmap_range() can folio_put the PTE's only reference before folio_set_hugetlb_migratable().\nPR:L - userfaultfd_syscall_allowed() accepts UFFD_USER_MODE_ONLY with no CAP_SYS_PTRACE, and ksys_mmap_pgoff() creates an anonymous MAP_HUGETLB file in hugetlb_file_setup() without can_do_hugetlb_shm(); UFFDIO_REGISTER only checks VM_MAYWRITE on that VMA.\nUI:N - The attacker mmaps the hugetlb range, registers userfaultfd, and races UFFDIO_COPY with MADV_DONTNEED in its own threads. No other task has to mount, open, or fault the mapping.\nS:U - folio_set_hugetlb_migratable() corrupts the folio free_huge_folio() already released from the caller's PTE. The result stays in that host's kernel address space, with no guest-to-host or IOMMU boundary crossed.\nC:H - MADV_DONTNEED's folio_put() in free_pages_and_swap_cache() calls free_huge_folio() on the PTE's only reference. A surplus page is then passed to free_frozen_pages(), whose set_buddy_order() stores the order in page->private, and the late set_bit(HPG_migratable) corrupts that reused struct page.\nI:H - folio_set_hugetlb_migratable() is set_bit(HPG_migratable, &folio->private) after the page-table reference is gone. On the hugepage freelist the next dequeue inherits the flag; if surplus_huge_pages_node[nid] is set, the same bit flips the buddy order written by set_buddy_order().\nA:H - hugetlb_unmap_range() drops the last reference and free_huge_folio() recycles the folio while hugetlb_mfill_atomic_pte() still writes it. Flipping the buddy order or a freelist folio's migratable flag faults the page allocator or a later fault on the reused page."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ],
            "affected": [
