    "containers": {
        "cna": {
            "providerMetadata": {
                "orgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
                "shortName": "Linux",
                "dateUpdated": "2026-11-23T08:03:42.231Z"
            },
            "descriptions": [
                {
                    "lang": "en",
                    "value": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: hackrf: fix use-after-free in hackrf_alloc_urbs() error path\n\nhackrf_alloc_urbs() frees the URBs it allocated so far when one\nallocation fails, but leaves the entries in dev->urb_list[] and\ndev->urbs_initialized untouched. The caller, hackrf_start_streaming(),\nthen calls hackrf_free_urbs() on the error path, which walks\ndev->urbs_initialized entries and calls usb_free_urb() a second time on\nthe already-freed URBs, causing a use-after-free (slab-use-after-free\nWrite in usb_free_urb()).\n\nDrop the redundant cleanup loop inside hackrf_alloc_urbs() and let\nhackrf_free_urbs(), which the caller already invokes on error, own the\ncleanup of the successfully allocated URBs."
                }
            ],
            "metrics": [
                {
                    "cvssV3_1": {
                        "version": "3.1",
                        "vectorString": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H",
                        "baseScore": 7,
                        "baseSeverity": "HIGH"
                    },
                    "scenarios": [
                        {
                            "lang": "en",
                            "value": "AV:L - hackrf_alloc_urbs() is reached only from hackrf_start_streaming(), which vb2_start_streaming() runs for VIDIOC_STREAMON (vb2_ioctl_streamon) or read()/write() (vb2_fop_read/vb2_fop_write) on the /dev/swradio node from video_register_device() in hackrf_probe(). The double-free is that error path when usb_alloc_urb() returns NULL; no USB packet or remote message carries the bad input.\nAC:H - The second usb_free_urb() happens only if usb_alloc_urb(0, GFP_KERNEL) fails for a later index after at least one success, and only after hackrf_alloc_stream_bufs() has already allocated six 64KB coherent buffers. An order-0 GFP_KERNEL failure after those costly DMA allocations is not a state the caller can produce on demand.\nPR:L - hackrf_fops.open is v4l2_fh_open and the VIDIOC_STREAMON path has no capable() check, so the gate is permission to open /dev/swradioN. The kernel creates that node mode 0600 and video4linux udev grants it to the video group and the active seat, which a normal local user has, without CAP_SYS_ADMIN.\nUI:N - The same process that opens /dev/swradioN calls VIDIOC_STREAMON or read()/write() and thereby hackrf_start_streaming(). hackrf_probe() stops after CMD_BOARD_ID_READ and CMD_VERSION_STRING_READ and never calls hackrf_alloc_urbs().\nS:U - kref_put() in the second usb_free_urb() corrupts a freed struct urb inside the kernel that handled the V4L2 ioctl, the same security authority as the caller.\nC:H - hackrf_free_urbs() calls usb_free_urb() on urb_list entries that hackrf_alloc_urbs() already freed, and kref_put() writes that freed struct urb. The object contains kernel pointers (transfer_buffer, dev, complete); reclaiming the slab slot turns the use-after-free into a kernel memory read.\nI:H - The second kref_put() writes the kref at the start of the freed urb, and if a reclaim leaves that word at 1, urb_destroy() kfree()s the object again and kfree()s transfer_buffer when URB_FREE_BUFFER is set.\nA:H - That kref_put() is a slab use-after-free write in usb_free_urb(). It corrupts allocator metadata or hits refcount saturation on the freed urb and oopses the kernel."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ],
