{
    "dataType": "CVE_RECORD",
    "dataVersion": "5.2",
    "cveMetadata": {
        "cveId": "CVE-2026-99535",
        "assignerOrgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
        "state": "PUBLISHED",
        "assignerShortName": "Linux",
        "dateReserved": "2026-09-25T10:25:14.420Z",
        "datePublished": "2026-11-19T14:44:48.628Z",
        "dateUpdated": "2026-11-23T08:03:59.397Z"
    },
    "containers": {
        "cna": {
            "providerMetadata": {
                "orgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
                "shortName": "Linux",
                "dateUpdated": "2026-11-23T08:03:59.397Z"
            },
            "descriptions": [
                {
                    "lang": "en",
                    "value": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: prevent share root removal through empty paths\n\nA FileLinkInformation request can supply \"/\" as the new link name.\nsmb2_get_name() strips the trailing slash and passes an empty string to\nksmbd_vfs_kern_path_start_removing().\n\nksmbd_vfs_path_lookup() resolves an empty pathname as the configured share\npath, without LOOKUP_BENEATH. With ReplaceIfExists set, smb2_create_link()\ncan therefore remove the share root from its parent before link creation\nfails. An authenticated client with a writable share and DELETE access to\na file can trigger this if the share root is empty and the mapped user\nhas write and search permission on its parent directory.\n\nReturn -EINVAL for empty pathnames when for_remove is set, before\nresolving the share path or acquiring removal resources. Ordinary lookups\ncontinue to accept empty pathnames for opening the share root."
                }
            ],
            "affected": [
                {
                    "product": "Linux",
