{
    "dataType": "CVE_RECORD",
    "dataVersion": "5.2",
    "cveMetadata": {
        "cveId": "CVE-2026-99549",
        "assignerOrgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
        "state": "PUBLISHED",
        "assignerShortName": "Linux",
        "dateReserved": "2026-09-25T10:25:14.421Z",
        "datePublished": "2026-11-19T14:45:13.123Z",
        "dateUpdated": "2026-11-23T08:04:14.102Z"
    },
    "containers": {
        "cna": {
            "providerMetadata": {
                "orgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
                "shortName": "Linux",
                "dateUpdated": "2026-11-23T08:04:14.102Z"
            },
            "descriptions": [
                {
                    "lang": "en",
                    "value": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: do not pass a NULL buf to is_oplock_break()\n\nreceive_encrypted_read() sets *num_mids = 1 and never writes the\ncaller's bufs[]. Offload returns -1 with *num_mids = 0, so the\ndemultiplex thread skips the frame. The inline decrypt path\nreturns 0 even when smb2_find_mid() fails.\n\ncifs_demultiplex_thread() then treats mids[i] == NULL as an\noplock break and calls is_oplock_break(bufs[i], server) with\nbufs[i] still NULL. smb2_is_valid_oplock_break() reads\nhdr.Command at offset 12 and oopses.\n\nA large encrypted READ whose MessageId does not match is enough\nto panic cifsd.\n\n    Oops: general protection fault, probably for non-canonical address\n    0xdffffc0000000001: 0000 [#1] SMP KASAN PTI\n    KASAN: null-ptr-deref in range\n    [0x0000000000000008-0x000000000000000f]\n    CPU: 0 PID: 100 Comm: cifsd\n    RIP: smb2_is_valid_oplock_break+0xc8/0x2270 [cifs]\n    cifs_demultiplex_thread\n    Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception\n\nReturn -1 when inline decrypt finds no mid, and skip\nis_oplock_break() plus the unknown-frame dump when bufs[i]\nis NULL. receive_encrypted_standard() already assigns\nbufs[*num_mids]."
                }
            ],
            "metrics": [
                {
                    "cvssV3_1": {
                        "version": "3.1",
                        "vectorString": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                        "baseScore": 7.5,
                        "baseSeverity": "HIGH"
                    },
                    "scenarios": [
                        {
                            "lang": "en",
                            "value": "AV:N - The triggering bytes are the SMB server's transform PDU. cifs_demultiplex_thread reads it with cifs_read_from_socket, smb3_is_transform_hdr matches ProtocolId SMB2_TRANSFORM_PROTO_NUM, and smb3_receive_transform calls receive_encrypted_read when pdu_size exceeds CIFSMaxBufSize+MAX_HEADER_SIZE. The decrypted smb2_hdr.MessageId misses pending_mid_q. SMB is routable TCP.\nAC:L - The server picks the cipher in negotiate so SMB2_sess_establish_session derives smb3decryptionkey, then sends one transform frame whose SessionId equals ses->Suid, whose OriginalMessageSize takes the inline path (min_offload is 0 unless esize= is set), and whose MessageId/Command pair smb2_find_mid misses. decrypt_raw_data returns 0, and the pre-fix function returns 0 with num_mids still 1.\nPR:N - cifs_demultiplex_thread applies no capability check to the peer. smb2_get_enc_key only matches tr_hdr->SessionId to ses->Suid of the session the client opened; the server does not authenticate to the client.\nUI:N - The frame is unsolicited. Once the session exists, cifs_demultiplex_thread reads the transform PDU and reaches smb2_is_valid_oplock_break with no VFS read or ioctl on that path. smb3_receive_transform selects receive_encrypted_read because pdu_size exceeds CIFSMaxBufSize+MAX_HEADER_SIZE.\nS:U - The NULL-pointer oops is in cifsd (cifs_demultiplex_thread) in the same kernel that holds the SMB session. It stays inside that kernel security boundary.\nC:N - smb2_is_valid_oplock_break loads rsp->hdr.Command at offset 12 through the NULL bufs[i] pointer and faults. The decrypted buffer is not copied to userspace.\nI:N - smb2_is_valid_oplock_break faults while loading rsp->hdr.Command through bufs[i], which receive_encrypted_read left NULL. That pointer is a zeroed stack slot rather than a value taken from the transform payload, so the oops supplies no write or control-flow primitive.\nA:H - The load in smb2_is_valid_oplock_break is a NULL-pointer general protection fault in the cifsd kthread. The fix commit's trace ends in a kernel panic (Fatal exception) from cifs_demultiplex_thread."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ],
